Not run: pull request from a fork

Pull requests from forks get a read-only `GITHUB_TOKEN` and no `id-token` permission, so the plan job can reach neither the AWS role nor the Stackorder server. Nothing was planned.

A maintainer can push the branch to this repository to plan it. Stackorder does not plan forks through `pull_request_target`, which would run untrusted code with this repository's credentials.
